2026-10-26 11:52:35.804 | 	--
2026-10-26 11:52:35.804 | 	-- A series already defines the pattern (subjects + question counts, optional
2026-10-26 11:52:35.804 | 	-- topic breakdown) and the marking scheme, so it now also holds its selected
2026-10-26 11:52:35.804 | 	-- questions directly and is what students sit.
2026-10-26 11:52:35.804 | 	--
2026-10-26 11:52:35.804 | 	--   paper_questions                   → series_questions
2026-10-26 11:52:35.804 | 	--   question_ingestion_jobs.target_paper_id → target_series_id
2026-10-26 11:52:35.804 | 	--   test_attempts.paper_id            → series_id
2026-10-26 11:52:35.804 | 	--   exam_papers                       → dropped
2026-10-26 11:52:35.804 | 	--
2026-10-26 11:52:35.804 | 	-- Backfill: each series takes the questions of its one paper that has any.
2026-10-26 11:52:35.804 | 	-- If a series has questions in more than one paper, the migration stops (no
2026-10-26 11:52:35.804 | 	-- guessing which to keep) — leave questions in one paper per series, re-run.
2026-10-26 11:52:35.804 | 	-- A published series that isn't complete afterwards goes back to draft, so
2026-10-26 11:52:35.804 | 	-- students never see a test with missing questions. Idempotent: safe to re-run.
